## What upgrade-legacy now does to `resource-map.md`

Nothing. The fill's eligibility gate (`runtime/cli/lib/frontmatter-migration.ts:943-945`) tests `SPEC_DOC_BASENAMES` or `TEMPLATE_DOC_FILES`; `resource-map.md` is in neither (the basename set ends at `handover.md`, and the template map has no entry since the addon template was deleted), so the file is skipped and returns byte-identical. Confirmed by the first observation run (byte-identity assertion passed) and re-asserted after hardening. Resulting frontmatter, quoted verbatim from the file:

```
---
title: "Authored Resource Map"
description: "An authored resource map."
importance_tier: "critical"
---
# Resource Map

Legacy map written before v4.
```

No `contextType` is added, no `_memory` block is added, and the tier is not duplicated.

